insert into public.cpl_memory (slug,kind,title,summary,tags,status,source,verified_by,verified_at,author,event_date) values
('r-handover-note-sam-2026-11-20','decision','The hand-over panel takes a note; a course''s note can say it is not in the catalog','Sam, 2026-11-20, in session: "the hand-over panel needs a place to leave a note. I got to Ohlone''s BRDC 127A, 127B, 127C and 127D and they are not in the catalog, but there is no place for me to note that." Built in S693: every box ends with Or leave a note; a course''s has one box, This course is not in the current catalog (kind note).',array['commons','hand-over','note','sam-ruling'],'verified','Sam, in session 2026-11-20 (S693, the plain session); docs/kb-notes/reference-commons-hand-over.md','Sam (in session)',now(),'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('r-handover-list-sam-2026-11-20','decision','Signed in, the hand-over box lists each thing handed over by name','Sam, 2026-11-20, after dropping seven term report CSVs one at a time: "it doesn''t show them all listed so confirm that each one i loaded did not overwrite the previous". Built in S693: a signed-in reviewer sees each file, link, pasted entry and note by name, with its time and what stands. No drop replaces another: each object''s name starts with a new id.',array['commons','hand-over','term-reports','sam-ruling'],'verified','Sam, in session 2026-11-20 (S693, the plain session); docs/kb-notes/reference-commons-hand-over.md','Sam (in session)',now(),'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('d-note-catalog-box-is-its-own-field-2026-11-20','decision','A course''s note carries not in the catalog as its own field','S693 (SkyKittiwake), 2026-11-20: a note is {text, not_in_catalog, source_url}. The box is its own field so the no-longer-offered check reads a person''s catalog finding with no sentence to parse. Nothing is set aside on a note alone (r-no-longer-offered-sam-2026-11-20: every factor agreeing). His to revise. Undo: the note migration''s rollback, which keeps every note written.',array['commons','hand-over','note','no-longer-offered'],'proposed','kb/migrations/2026-11-20_commons_handover_note.sql; commons_handover.js; tests/commons_handover_note_sql_proof.py',null,null,'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('p-try-link-503-no-reason-2026-11-20','pitfall','Try the link answered 503 three times and nothing recorded why','Sam''s three Try the link presses (2026-11-20, 19:37 to 19:41Z) each got 503 from handover-try-link, so no pickup run started and the page said only that the link waits. The edge log keeps the status alone: not_configured and token_refused could not be told apart. Since S693 the function logs its reason and the page names it. A session can dispatch commons-handover-pickup.yml on main itself.',array['commons','hand-over','edge-function','pitfall'],'proposed','Supabase function_edge_logs 2026-11-20; chatbox/supabase/functions/handover-try-link/index.ts; run 44806543827',null,null,'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20'),
('m-first-real-hand-overs-2026-11-20','milestone','Sam''s first real hand-overs: 3 links, 8 pasted entries, 7 term reports','2026-11-20: Sam handed over 3 catalog links (all read, HTTP 200 with no challenge, run 44806543827), 8 pasted catalog descriptions for still-taught courses, and 7 term report CSVs (251,470 rows in all, 18 columns each with a Term column; run 44808354149). The private store took a reviewer''s upload on its INSERT policy alone, and seven drops are seven objects.',array['commons','hand-over','term-reports','milestone'],'proposed','commons_handover live read 2026-11-20; runs 44806543827 and 44808354149',null,null,'SkyKittiwake (S693)','2026-11-20')
on conflict (slug) do nothing;

